// Host <-> guest agent protocol (forkbox-agent, over vsock).
//
// Framing: every message is a 4-byte big-endian length followed by that many
// bytes of a serialized Request (host to guest) or Response (guest to host).
// Frames larger than 1 MiB are refused.
//
// One operation per connection. The host connects, sends one Request with
// the operation, and reads Responses until a terminal one; then either side
// closes. Vsock connections are reset by snapshots, so nothing is kept on a
// connection between operations, and a new connection is all a restored VM
// needs.
//
//   ping       -> pong
//   exec       -> exec_started, output*, exec_exit
//   signal     -> signal
//   read_file  -> file_header, chunk*, file_done
//   write_file -> (host sends chunk* with the last one eof) -> file_done
//   stat       -> stat
//   wait_port  -> wait_port
//   info       -> info
//   restored   -> restored
//
// Any operation may end with `error` instead.

